-- title:
--   Abel's theorem on ΓbackslashH^*: necessity
-- statement:
--   Let $\Gamma \le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ be a subgroup of finite index, let $c : \mathfrak{H} \to \mathbb{Z}$ be a finitely supported function on the upper half plane, and let $F : \mathfrak{H} \to \mathbb{C}$ satisfy: the function $z \mapsto F(\mathtt{ofComplex}\,z)$ on $\mathbb{C}$ is meromorphic at every point $\tau \in \mathfrak{H}$; $F(\gamma\tau) = F(\tau)$ for all $\gamma \in \Gamma$ and all $\tau$; for every $\sigma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ the function $\tau \mapsto F(\sigma\tau)$ tends, along the filter $\mathrm{Im}\,\tau \to \infty$, to some limit $L \neq 0$; and, for every $\tau \in \mathfrak{H}$, the meromorphic order of $z \mapsto F(\mathtt{ofComplex}\,z)$ at $\tau$, as an element of $\mathbb{Z} \cup \{\infty\}$, equals the integer $e_\tau \cdot \bar c(\Gamma\tau)$, where $e_\tau$ is the natural-number quotient by $2$ of the cardinality of the stabiliser of $\tau$ in the subgroup $\Gamma \sqcup \langle -1 \rangle$ generated by $\Gamma$ and $-1$, and $\bar c$ is the push-forward of $c$ along the quotient map $\mathfrak{H} \to \Gamma\backslash\mathfrak{H}$ for the orbit relation, evaluated at the orbit of $\tau$. Then the functional $\sum_{\tau} c(\tau)\,\pi_\tau$ on weight-two cusp forms for $\Gamma$, the sum running over the support of $c$, where $\pi_\tau(f) = \int_0^1 f(\gamma_{i,\tau}(t))\,(\tau - i)\,dt$ is integration of $f$ along the segment path from $i$ to $\tau$, lies in the period lattice of $\Gamma$, i.e. the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of the dual of $\mathrm{CuspForm}\,\Gamma\,2$ spanned by the functionals $f \mapsto \int_i^{\gamma i} f$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma$.
--
--   This is the necessity direction of Abel's theorem for the modular curve $X(\Gamma) = \Gamma\backslash\mathfrak{H}^*$, formulated entirely on the upper half plane: $F$ plays the role of a meromorphic function on $X(\Gamma)$ which is a unit at every cusp and whose divisor is $\sum \bar c(\Gamma\tau)[\Gamma\tau]$, the factor $e_\tau$ converting vanishing orders in the coordinate on $\mathfrak{H}$ into orders in a local parameter at a possibly elliptic point, and the conclusion states that the Abel–Jacobi image of that divisor vanishes modulo periods. It is used in the treatment of principal divisors on the curves $X_H$, via [`ModularCurve.ComplexPlaceDictionaryOf.abelJacobi_mem_periodLatticeOf_gammaH_of_isPrincipal`](thm.html#ModularCurve.ComplexPlaceDictionaryOf.abelJacobi_mem_periodLatticeOf_gammaH_of_isPrincipal).
